{'review': '{\n  "review": "<<<ARTIFACT review_report>>>\\n{\\n  \\"overall_status\\": \\"NEEDS_FIXES\\",\\n  \\"quality_score\\": 6.0,\\n  \\"summary\\": {\\n    \\"critical\\": 0,\\n    \\"high\\": 2,\\n    \\"medium\\": 1,\\n    \\"low\\": 2,\\n    \\"passed_checks\\": [\\"No hardcoded secrets\\", \\"JWT authentication configured\\", \\"All endpoints authorized\\", \\"Dependency injection used correctly\\", \\"Global exception handler logs errors\\"]\\n  },\\n  \\"findings\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\"finding_id\\": \\"F-001\\",\\n      \\"severity\\": \\"high\\",\\n      \\"category\\": \\"quality\\",\\n      \\"title\\": \\"Missing GET endpoint for individual todo resource\\",\\n      \\"file\\": \\"src/Api/Program.cs\\",\\n      \\"line_range\\": [68, 78],\\n      \\"description\\": "The CreateTodo endpoint uses Results.CreatedAtRoute with route name \\"GetAllTodos\\" and an id parameter, but no endpoint exists for getting a single todo by ID. This will cause an exception when generating the Location header for 201 responses.",\\n      "impact": "Runtime failure when creating a todo item: InvalidOperationException due to missing route values for the GetAllTodos route.",\\n      "suggested_fix": "Either add a GET /v1/todos/{id} endpoint or change to Results.Created with explicit URL.",\\n      "code_before": "return Results.CreatedAtRoute(\\"GetAllTodos\\", new { id = result.Value.Id }, result.Value);",\\n      "code_after": "return Results.Created($\\"/v1/todos/{result.Value.Id}\\", result.Value);",\\n      "references": []\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\"finding_id\\": \\"F-002\\",\\n      \\"severity\\": \\"high\\",\\n      \\"category\\": \\"security\\",\\n      \\"title\\": "JWT token validation missing null checks for Issuer/Audience",\\n      "file": "src/Api/Program.cs",\\n      "line_range": [30, 40],\\n      "description": "The JWT validation parameters set ValidateIssuer and ValidateAudience to true, but the corresponding configuration values (Jwt:Issuer, Jwt:Audience) are not validated for null presence during startup. If missing, validation will fail at runtime for all tokens.",\\n      "impact": "Application starts successfully but all authenticated requests will return 401 Unauthorized due to token validation failure, causing authentication bypass for legitimate users.",\\n      "suggested_fix": "Add startup validation for JWT Issuer and Audience when validation is enabled, similar to the existing secret key check.",\\n      "code_before": "    options.TokenValidationParameters = new TokenValidationParameters\\n    {\\n        ValidateIssuer = true,\\n        ValidateAudience = true,\\n        ValidateLifetime = true,\\n        ValidateIssuerSigningKey = true,\\n        ValidIssuer = builder.Configuration[\\"Jwt:Issuer\\"],\\n        ValidAudience = builder.Configuration[\\"Jwt:Audience\\"],\\n        IssuerSigningKey = new SymmetricSecurityKey(Encoding.UTF8.GetBytes(jwtSecret))\\n    };",\\n      "code_after": "    var jwtIssuer = builder.Configuration[\\"Jwt:Issuer\\"] ?? throw new InvalidOperationException(\\"JWT Issuer not configured.\\");\\n    var jwtAudience = builder.Configuration[\\"Jwt:Audience\\"] ?? throw new InvalidOperationException(\\"JWT Audience not configured.\\");\\n    \\n    options.TokenValidationParameters = new TokenValidationParameters\\n    {\\n        ValidateIssuer = true,\\n        ValidateAudience = true,\\n        ValidateLifetime = true,\\n        ValidateIssuerSigningKey = true,\\n        ValidIssuer = jwtIssuer,\\n        ValidAudience = jwtAudience,\\n        IssuerSigningKey = new SymmetricSecurityKey(Encoding.UTF8.GetBytes(jwtSecret))\\n    };",\\n      "references": ["CWE-287: Improper Authentication", "OWASP A02:2021 - Cryptographic Failures"]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      "finding_id\\": \\"F-003\\",\\n      \\"severity\\": \\"medium\\",\\n      \\"category\\": \\"quality\\",\\n      \\"title\\": "Global exception handler hides detailed errors in development",\\n      "file": "src/Api/Program.cs",\\n      "line_range": [45, 58],\\n      "description": "The custom exception handler returns a generic error message in all environments, preventing developers from seeing detailed exception information during debugging when using the API directly (outside of Swagger).",\\n      "impact": "Increased debugging difficulty in development environments as root cause of exceptions is not visible to callers.",\\n      "suggested_fix": "Conditionally show detailed errors in development while maintaining generic messages in production.",\\n      "code_before": "app.UseExceptionHandler(exceptionHandlerApp =>\\n{\\n    exceptionHandlerApp.Run(async context =>\\n    {\\n        var exceptionHandlerPathFeature = context.Features.Get<IExceptionHandlerPathFeature>();\\n        var exception = exceptionHandlerPathFeature?.Error;\\n\\n        // Log the exception details\\n        var logger = context.RequestServices.GetRequiredService<ILogger<Program>>();\\n        logger.LogError(exception, \\"An unhandled exception occurred: {Message}\\", exception?.Message);\\n\\n        context.Response.StatusCode = StatusCodes.Status500InternalServerError;\\n        await context.Response.WriteAsync(\\"An unexpected error occurred.\\");\\n    });\\n});",\\n      "code_after": "if (app.Environment.IsDevelopment())\\n{\\n    app.UseDeveloperExceptionPage();\\n}\\nelse\\n{\\n    app.UseExceptionHandler(exceptionHandlerApp =>\\n    {\\n        exceptionHandlerApp.Run(async context =>\\n        {\\n            var exceptionHandlerPathFeature = context.Features.Get<IExceptionHandlerPathFeature>();\\n            var exception = exceptionHandlerPathFeature?.Error;\\n\\n            // Log the exception details\\n            var logger = context.RequestServices.GetRequiredService<ILogger<Program>>();\\n            logger.LogError(exception, \\"An unhandled exception occurred: {Message}\\", exception?.Message);\\n\\n            context.Response.StatusCode = StatusCodes.Status500InternalServerError;\\n            await context.Response.WriteAsync(\\"An unexpected error occurred.\\");\\n        });\\n    });\\n}",\\n      "references": []\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\"finding_id\\": \\"F-004\\",\\n      \\"severity\\": \\"low\\",\\n      \\"category\\": \\"quality\\",\\n      \\"title\\": "Inconsistent error response format (plain text vs JSON)",\\n      "file": "src/Api/Program.cs",\\n      "line_range": [72, 74],\\n      "description": "Error responses return plain text strings (e.g., Results.BadRequest(result.Error)) while successful responses return JSON objects. This creates inconsistency in API contract that may break client expectations.",\\n      "impact": "Clients must handle multiple response formats (text/plain for errors, application/json for success), increasing complexity and risk of parsing errors.",\\n      "suggested_fix": "Return consistent JSON error responses using a standard error object or ProblemDetails.",\\n      "code_before": "return Results.BadRequest(result.Error);",\\n      "code_after": "return Results.BadRequest(new { error = result.Error });",\\n      "references": []\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\"finding_id\\": \\"F-005\\",\\n      \\"severity\\": \\"low\\",\\n      \\"category\\": \\"quality\\",\\n      \\"title\\": "Redundant Produces status code comments",\\n      "file": "src/Api/Program.cs",\\n      "line_range": [80, 85],\\n      "description": "Comments indicating removed Produces attributes (F-005 fixes) are no longer relevant and clutter the code.",\\n      "impact": "Reduces code readability and maintainability.",\\n      "suggested_fix": "Remove outdated comments about removed Produces attributes.",\\n      "code_before": ".Produces<TodoResponse>(StatusCodes.Status201Created); // F-005 fix: Removed .Produces(StatusCodes.Status400BadRequest)",\\n      "code_after": ".Produces<TodoResponse>(StatusCodes.Status201Created);",\\n      "references": []\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\"positive_observations\\": [\\n    \\"JWT authentication properly configured with secret validation and token parameters\\",\\n    \\"All endpoints correctly protected with [Authorize] attribute\\",\\n    \\"Result pattern used consistently for service layer responses\\",\\n    \\"Dependency injection correctly applied for services and DbContext factory\\",\\n    \\"Global exception handler logs full exception details while returning generic client messages\\",\\n    \\"Swagger enabled in development for API documentation and testing\\"\\n  ]\\n}\\n<<<ENDARTIFACT>>>"}'}